DRAFT FOR REVIEW, untested: /etc/pam.d/su and /etc/pam.d/ file events (Fragnesia artefact).
Needs Sysmon for Linux, auditd, or an EDR sourcetype that maps file path fields.
Hunt ID: 2026-10-28-php2shell-fragnesia-chain | ATT&CK: T1068, T1556.003
Source: https://github.com/CyberThreatNet/hunt-lab | Licence: MIT
Adjust index/sourcetype to your estate. Field names below are illustrative.
```
| search (index=* OR index=_*) ("/etc/pam.d/su" OR "/etc/pam.d/")
| where like(file_path, "%/etc/pam.d/%") OR like(TargetFilename, "%/etc/pam.d/%") OR like(file_name, "su")
| stats count min(_time) as FirstSeen max(_time) as LastSeen values(user) as Users
    by dest, file_path, TargetFilename, action, process_name
| convert ctime(FirstSeen) ctime(LastSeen)
| sort - LastSeen
